  "notes": "The six stepped stone masses of Kumsusan Palace include the rounded west gallery, a recessed north colonnade and twin stylized portrait panels. The mapped terrace walls, approach stairs and two four-quadrant ornamental fountains complete the formal forecourt. The six plan shapes and mapped height bands fix the exterior massing. The finished floor, stone terrace and small fittings are visual estimates from the exterior photos and Terrarium grades. The palace and formal forecourt are represented as exterior architecture. The memorial portraits and fountain figures use stylized geometry. Coarse native relief around the rear service paths rises against the lower wing in the rear view.",
